From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:01:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] bt-a: let A2DP take audio focus, from the product overlay

A2DP is selectable but silent: the Bluetooth app's
a2dp_sink_automatically_request_audio_focus is false in AOSP, so the
stack requests no focus for it and the route never becomes active.
Set it to true in this device's overlay instead of patching the
Bluetooth module's config.xml. DEFAULT-DIALER.md now says where the
value lives, and README.md lists the overlay and counts its value
among the ones that stay.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending [automotive-grade-linux/Android_device_sodev_xenvm-cf]
---
